course: dictionary
lesson: 13276
title: Gospels: good news, good book, good music
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. The clues around it tell you which one is meant. «The Gospels tell the story of Jesus, and our class reads them in RE.» The word «Gospels» has a capital G, and the words «tell the story of Jesus» show it means the books of the Bible.
explain: «The gospel choir sang so loudly that the windows shook.» Choir is your clue. A gospel choir is a group of singers, so gospel here means a lively style of Christian singing.
explain: «When Mum says the recipe works, I take it as gospel.» Mum is not talking about a book or a church. Take it as gospel means believe it totally, so it is an informal way to say something is completely true.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. If «believe it totally» still makes sense in «I take it as gospel», you have found the right meaning.
fact: The Gospels are the first four books of the New Testament, written by Matthew, Mark, Luke and John.
fact: The Gospels tell the life and teaching of Jesus.
fact: «The gospel» means the Christian message, the «good news» about Jesus.
fact: Gospel music is a lively style of Christian singing from African American churches, often with clapping and strong voices.
fact: «Gospel truth» or «take it as gospel» means something is completely true.
exercise: «The four Gospels tell the story of Jesus' life.» What are the Gospels? | Four famous churches in one city | Four songs sung in church on Sunday | *The first four books of the New Testament, by Matthew, Mark, Luke and John | Four stories about dragons from an old book
exercise: «The gospel choir clapped and sang with strong voices.» What kind of music is this? | Silent music with no sound at all | Opera, sung by one person on a stage | Nursery rhymes for very young children | *Gospel music, a lively style of Christian singing
exercise: «When Grandma says the recipe works, I take it as gospel.» What does take it as gospel mean? | Throw it away | Cook it slowly | Read it aloud to everyone | *Believe it totally
test: «In RE we read the Gospel of Luke and talk about what Jesus taught.» What does gospel mean here? | A school report card | A kind of loud, lively dance | A sort of cake made with honey | *The Christian message, the good news about Jesus
test: «The Nativity story is found in the Gospels.» Where are the Gospels found? | In a library of old newspapers | In a cookbook on the kitchen shelf | *In the New Testament of the Bible | In the school music room
exam: In «The choir sang gospel songs with clapping and joy», what does gospel mean? | A small church bell | The first four books of the Bible | Something that is completely true | *A lively style of Christian singing
